      "displayName": "Andrew Woods",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=60785ded115da6006f540529",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>I was able to get the one-click to run without having to pass in the jetty.xml file as a jar argument, but then ran into the next issue of the jetty.xml using a HashLoginService which also expects a file (as opposed to an InputStream).</p>\n\n<p>All things considered, this ticket should ensure that the one-click is able to run, but not with AuthZ.</p>",
